  "request_sha256": "2d6444dd69054da0e19cfbc3c06103dbebd4acec507e48a0298eeb7d90940850",
  "response": {
    "data": {
      "A": "Research the prefix-frequency counting kernel, initially keeping traversal and execution serial to isolate its effect. Compare a reserved unordered_map using one find result against a reusable flat open-addressed table. A scan of length L stores at most L+1 distinct prefixes, including zero: size the table accordingly with a conservative load factor, exact key comparisons and unsigned hash arithmetic that handles negative keys. Missing-key queries must not insert entries. Allocate workspace outside band loops; compare generation tags with clearing occupancy/count storage, including their initialization costs. For every band, seed frequency[0]=1, query frequency[s-k] before incrementing frequency[s], and retain 64-bit sum/query arithmetic and answers. Small frequency counters are safe because each frequency is at most L+1. Preserve the ordered-prefix algorithm rather than counting unordered prefix pairs. Deliver the best independently measured program and a counting kernel that G can reuse with contiguous scans and worker-private storage.",
      "B": "Research dimension choice and memory locality while initially retaining the reference counting method. Let S=min(m,n) and L=max(m,n); enumerate boundary pairs along S and scan along L, reducing work to O(S²L). Orient the matrix as X[S][L] and build P[t+1][r]=P[t][r]+X[t][r], with P[0] zero. Store each P[t] contiguously so a band [a,b] supplies P[b+1][r]-P[a][r] through two sequential streams instead of the baseline's strided accesses. Compare this against incrementally extending a contiguous band-sum buffer for each starting boundary; measure rather than assuming either layout wins. Include preprocessing and allocation in end-to-end timing. As a separate inexpensive variant, disable unnecessary iostream synchronization/ties and avoid clearing unused matrix capacity while preserving initialized prefix boundaries. Keep all signed values and rectangular shapes correct. Deliver the winning layout and clearly state whether bands are independently addressable or require incremental extension, since this constrains C's scheduling.",
      "C": "Research balanced CPU parallelism on the fixed four-core ARM64 target using threading facilities supported by the unchanged build. Each boundary pair is independent when endpoint prefixes are available. Compare coarse, balanced ranges of flattened boundary pairs against coarse dynamic scheduling; avoid naively dividing starting boundaries equally because their remaining work decreases triangularly. If using incremental band buffers, schedule complete starting-boundary tasks with weights proportional to their number of ending boundaries. Every worker must own its frequency table, any band buffer and a 64-bit partial answer; share only immutable input/prefix data and reduce once after workers finish. Avoid inner-loop atomics, shared maps, per-band thread creation and per-band allocation. Within the existing measurement allowance, assess serial, two-worker and four-worker variants. Retain a low-overhead serial path for small estimated work S(S+1)L/2, chosen from measurements rather than test identities. Report startup, scheduling and private-workspace costs through full-program timings.",
      "G": "Integrate measured programs from A/B/C, retaining the best standalone candidate as a fallback. Prioritize measuring A+B serially, then adding the compatible C scheduler; use remaining permitted measurements for targeted ablations if integration regresses. Do not add component speedups or assume a combined program is faster. Reconcile dimensions before sizing frequency tables: capacity depends on scan length L after orientation. Match scheduling to B's representation, initialize every worker's table correctly, and keep partial and final counts 64-bit. Review negative values, repeated prefixes, k=0, one-dimensional matrices and maximum counts without modifying the supplied tests. Run the unchanged correctness gate and timing protocol on each candidate considered for selection, especially the exact final integrated artifact. Four passing baseline cases are evidence, not proof of correctness over all valid inputs. Select by the existing objective and retain a simpler measured variant when integration loses. Do not change tests, oracle, compiler configuration, budgets, target or permissions.",
      "analysis": "Only Problem A matches the supplied source; A/B/C are research roles, not the other contest problems. The baseline passes four correctness cases and averages 0.249729 seconds across three closely spaced timing samples. No input dimensions, value distributions or hotspot measurements are supplied, so proposed gains remain hypotheses. The source exposes O(m*n²) traversal, strided prefix accesses, repeated unordered_map clearing/allocation and redundant successful lookups. The complementary priorities are cheaper frequency counting, pairing the smaller dimension with contiguous scans, and balanced parallel execution on four CPU cores. Negative entries rule out a general sliding-window replacement. The answer can reach 249500250000, requiring 64-bit accumulation. All variants must preserve the empty-prefix seed and query-before-insertion ordering so only non-empty submatrices are counted. Evaluate end-to-end costs, including preprocessing and thread startup, rather than kernel throughput alone."
    },
